**Read:** [Principles of Extractive Metallurgy — Tarun Kumar Kundu, NPTEL](../sources/Principles-of-Extractive-Metallurgy-NPTEL.lingua#r_7VCNEHN5VCQDDQTZ512PSHFZ78), the entire course and full primary methods used; [Non-ferrous Extractive Metallurgy — Ray and Pugazhenthy, NPTEL](../sources/Nonferrous-Extractive-Metallurgy-NPTEL.lingua#r_29G1ZF58Y8EG123MNX3ZRNRE2W), the complete applicable theoretical and metal-family progression; [Materials, energy, and heat balances in metallurgical processes — Satish Ch. Koria](../sources/Metallurgical-Material-and-Heat-Balances-NPTEL.lingua#r_38NWQRDJH3RVM3NNGB71RR1X43), all relevant full derivations and worked cases; [Non-ferrous Metals Industries — European Commission BREF](../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB), whole relevant process/metal-family chapters and actual comparison cases.

Select a documented target metal/feed and at least two substantive extraction/refining arrangements using different combinations of thermal, solution, and electrochemical duties where scientifically suitable. Read the full unit-process courses, complete relevant technical chapters, and original method papers. State what feed, product, utility, residual, operating, or proprietary information remains unavailable.

Construct compatible phase/chemical, material/charge, thermal, kinetic/transport, reactor, and separation accounts. Derive the governing relations and use exact assessed/evaluated data with their reference states and domains. Distinguish fitted parameters from independent observations and state identifiability, uncertainty, and numerical limitations.

Reproduce a substantial published result and validate against another feed/condition or a carefully scoped independent supplied-data case. Verify reaction/element/charge balance, nonnegativity, equilibrium/rate limits, numerical convergence, and consistency of heat/work and inventory. Test impurity accumulation, feed variability, and a consequential utility/equipment interruption.

**Work:** defend the competing routes on accepted product, recovery/selectivity, energy/water/reagents, residuals, equipment/containment, maintenance, and human work. Trace a consequential discrepancy across process boundaries and compare two possible explanations. Specify the laboratory/pilot or operating investigation most likely to change the design. A mathematical balance or favorable equilibrium is treated as evidence within a whole process, with practical competence described by the actual work performed.

**Continue:** [Defend a complete iron/steel route from variable feed to specified product and residuals](Advanced-iron-and-steel-production-and-product-study.lingua#r_5RKJ2VSR6KN1HZSV61FK90RX34).

